WEBVTT

00:00.500 --> 00:07.187
The Pythagorean theorem is about right triangles. A right triangle has one square corner.

00:07.637 --> 00:14.383
The two shorter sides are called the legs. The longest side, across from the square corner,

00:14.383 --> 00:15.718
is the hypotenuse.

00:16.168 --> 00:22.563
Take a triangle with legs three and four. Square each leg. Three squared is nine.

00:22.563 --> 00:24.457
Four squared is sixteen.

00:24.907 --> 00:31.873
Add the squares. Nine plus sixteen is twenty-five. That equals the longest side squared.

00:32.323 --> 00:38.509
What number times itself is twenty-five? It is five. So the longest side is five.

00:38.509 --> 00:42.633
The rule is a squared plus b squared equals c squared.
